p('The all-equal start (0.5,...,0.5) is also special: exact trajectories remain synchronous. At Lin\'s baseline the uniform eigenvalue is -1 while the transverse leading real part is +0.206011. Such a trajectory can converge to an equilibrium that repels generic perturbations. Disagreement with nonsynchronous starts does not establish coexisting attractors. Near-synchronous randomized starts and convergence checks are needed for a basin study.')
